! Written disabled, matching nothing:
!   firewall 1 (Banned by fail2ban): not converted: set @banned, which is filled at run time (flags timeout)
!   firewall 4 (Guests stay in): zones eth1, eth0: a policy names the interfaces lan, wan1, wan2 or all (give --zone-map ZONE=lan|wan1|wan2)
!   firewall 5 (LAN web): zones eth1, eth0: a policy names the interfaces lan, wan1, wan2 or all (give --zone-map ZONE=lan|wan1|wan2)
!   firewall 6 (LAN DNS): zones eth1, eth0: a policy names the interfaces lan, wan1, wan2 or all (give --zone-map ZONE=lan|wan1|wan2)
!   firewall 7 (Rate limited mail): not converted: rate limit 10/minute; zones eth1, eth0: a policy names the interfaces lan, wan1, wan2 or all (give --zone-map ZONE=lan|wan1|wan2)
!   firewall 8 (Partner tunnel): zones eth1, eth0: a policy names the interfaces lan, wan1, wan2 or all (give --zone-map ZONE=lan|wan1|wan2); IP protocol 47: a policy names all, TCP, UDP or ICMP
!   firewall 9 (Admins): zones eth1, eth2: a policy names the interfaces lan, wan1, wan2 or all (give --zone-map ZONE=lan|wan1|wan2)
!   firewall 10 (Ping the DMZ): zones eth1, eth2: a policy names the interfaces lan, wan1, wan2 or all (give --zone-map ZONE=lan|wan1|wan2); an ICMP type or code: a policy matches every ICMP message or none
!   firewall 11 (SCADA to PLCs): zones eth1, eth3: a policy names the interfaces lan, wan1, wan2 or all (give --zone-map ZONE=lan|wan1|wan2)
!   firewall 12 (OT no internet): zones eth3, eth0: a policy names the interfaces lan, wan1, wan2 or all (give --zone-map ZONE=lan|wan1|wan2)
!   firewall 13 (Inbound web): zones eth0, eth2: a policy names the interfaces lan, wan1, wan2 or all (give --zone-map ZONE=lan|wan1|wan2)
!   firewall 14 (Inbound mail): zones eth0, eth2: a policy names the interfaces lan, wan1, wan2 or all (give --zone-map ZONE=lan|wan1|wan2)
!   firewall 15 (Inbound IPv6): zones eth0, eth2: a policy names the interfaces lan, wan1, wan2 or all (give --zone-map ZONE=lan|wan1|wan2)
!   firewall 16 (DMZ updates): zones eth2, eth0: a policy names the interfaces lan, wan1, wan2 or all (give --zone-map ZONE=lan|wan1|wan2)
!   firewall 17 (ICMPv6 basics): no service the router's IPv4 policies can match
